cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Kapso in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Kapso: an engine that runs experiments, deploys the best solution and learns from every run"
abstract: >-
  Kapso is an open-source engine that runs experiments, deploys the best
  solution and learns from every run. It starts from a domain harness and
  an empty bank of lessons; given an objective and success criteria, it
  runs a tree of experiments, proposing hypotheses, then implementing and
  verifying each one, and deploys the best solution on the target stack.
  It then learns from the run, assigning credit to each hypothesis and
  implementation by its impact on the outcome and updating the bank, where
  every lesson carries a credence score and a boundary on where it applies.
